### Checking SurroundingText capability and deleteSurroundingText vs forwardKey BackSpace

Source: https://github.com/fcitx/fcitx5/blob/master/src/im/keyboard/keyboard.cpp

In keyboard.cpp, when processing a long press with an empty buffer, the code checks if the client supports SurroundingText. If yes, it calls deleteSurroundingText(-1, 1) to delete one character before the cursor. Otherwise it falls back to forwarding a BackSpace key event to the client. This is the clearest example of how capabilityFlags, SurroundingText, deleteSurroundingText, and forwardKey with BackSpace interact in the Fcitx 5 source.

```cpp
            if (inputContext->capabilityFlags().test(
                    CapabilityFlag::SurroundingText)) {
                inputContext->deleteSurroundingText(-1, 1);
            } else {
                inputContext->forwardKey(Key(FcitxKey_BackSpace));
            }
```

